<section #sec:inline-display-math | Inline & Display Math>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Math is written in LaTeX and rendered by KaTeX. Inline math sits in the line with `<$ … $>` (or `$…$`); display math is centred on its own line with `<$$ … $$>` (or `$$…$$`).

Inline: `<$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $>` or `$a^2 + b^2 = c^2$`
Display: `<$$ … $$>` or `$$ … $$`

<code #code:math-basic>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles, and

<$$ \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X $$>

sets the sum on its own line.
</code>

<minipage #mp:math-basic>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles, and

<$$ \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X $$>

sets the sum on its own line.
</minipage>

<sub-section | Notes>

`<math> … </math>` is a long-form alternative to `<$$ … $$>` for a display block. Give display math an id — `<$$ #eq:pythagoras | … $$>` — to cross-reference it.
</section>

<section #sec:aligned-equations | Aligned Equations>

<sub-section | General Usage>

`<align>` lines up a sequence of equations on a chosen column. Mark the alignment point with `&` and end each line with `\\`.

<code #code:align-basic>
<align>
(a + b)^2 &= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\
(a - b)^2 &= a^2 - 2ab + b^2
</align>
</code>

<minipage #mp:align-basic>
<align>
(a + b)^2 &= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\
(a - b)^2 &= a^2 - 2ab + b^2
</align>
</minipage>

<sub-section | Notes>

`<eqnarray>` is the relational variant, aligning on a central relation written `&=&`.
</section>

<section #sec:cases | Cases>

<sub-section | General Usage>

`<cases>` sets a piecewise definition. Each line is a value, a `&`, then its condition, ended with `\\`.

<code #code:cases-basic>
<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{if } x < 0
</cases>
</code>

<minipage #mp:cases-basic>
<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{if } x < 0
</cases>
</minipage>
</section>

<section #sec:matrices | Matrices>

<sub-section | General Usage>

`<matrix>` lays out a grid of entries. Separate columns with `&` and rows with `\\`.

<code #code:matrix-basic>
<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>
</code>

<minipage #mp:matrix-basic>
<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>
</minipage>
</section>
